    "note": "Sourced from the Sri Chaitanya Junior Fastrack zoology section, SAQ chapter 8 'Locomotion & Reproduction' (book p.42, question 41), which prints the labelled figure with NO written answer and NO year citation — so appearances are empty by fact, not by omission. Zoology holds only ONE source book — the TSBIE Basic Learning Material in hand covers physics only, and no zoology board paper is in the corpus — so the two-book union check and the past-paper back-test are both STRUCTURALLY IMPOSSIBLE for this card, not merely unrun; 'not checked' must never be read as 'checked and clean'. The mark split is this card's claim until a Telangana IPE teacher confirms it. TEXT BEYOND THE BOOK: the book prints the figure alone; the two written steps here are authored from the labels the book itself prints. FIGURE SCOPE: the book labels fifteen parts — long flagellum, cytostome, cytopharynx, stigma, paraflagellar body, reservoir, short flagellum, blepharoplast, contractile vacuole, chromatophores, paramylum, myonemes, nucleus, pellicle and cytoplasm. This figure draws and labels thirteen of them. CYTOPLASM and MYONEMES are deliberately not labelled: cytoplasm is the whole ground substance and needs no leader line at exam scale, and the myonemes are fine strips under the pellicle that crowd the pellicle label. A teacher who wants both can add them on the left body wall."
