          "Euglena is a spindle-shaped single-celled",
          "organism with a blunt anterior end and a",
          "pointed posterior end.",
          "The body is covered by a flexible pellicle.",
          "The drawing must show the anterior reservoir",
          "with the two flagella, the stigma beside it,",
          "the contractile vacuole, the chromatophores,",
          "the paramylum granules and the nucleus."
        ],
        "why": "Naming the shape and listing the parts before drawing fixes the order of work, so the anterior structures are placed first and the body contents afterwards.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Drawing a round cell. Euglena is spindle-shaped, blunt in front and pointed behind.",
          "Drawing the flagella at the pointed end. They come out of the reservoir at the BLUNT anterior end."
