        "why": "The figure is built from the front backwards, because every anterior structure is placed against the reservoir and would have nowhere to sit if the body contents were drawn first.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Drawing one flagellum. There are two, one long and one short.",
          "Placing the stigma inside the reservoir. It lies in the cytoplasm beside the reservoir.",
          "Drawing the nucleus at the anterior end. It lies towards the middle or the posterior half."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Draw the outline, then the reservoir and its flagella, then the stigma and vacuole, then the body contents, then label.",
        "margin_note": "Two marks sit here. Both flagella, the reservoir, the stigma and the nucleus decide them."
