        "lines": [
          {
            "text": "Reservoir, two flagella, stigma, nucleus",
            "style": "boxed"
          },
          "The two flagella arise from blepharoplasts at",
          "the base of the reservoir. One is long, one",
          "is short.",
          "The reservoir opens outside through the",
          "cytopharynx and the cytostome.",
          "The stigma is the orange eye spot. The",
          "paraflagellar body on the long flagellum is",
          "the light-sensitive part.",
          "The contractile vacuole beside the reservoir",
          "removes excess water.",
          "The chromatophores hold chlorophyll and the",
          "paramylum granules store food."
        ],
        "why": "Each label is easier to remember with the one job it does, and a single job line per part is also what an examiner accepts as a full description under a diagram.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Calling the stigma the light-sensitive part. The stigma shades the light; the paraflagellar body detects it.",
          "Writing that paramylum is a protein. It is a stored carbohydrate."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Front group: reservoir, flagella, blepharoplast, stigma, paraflagellar body, contractile vacuole. Body group: chromatophores, paramylum, nucleus.",
        "margin_note": "One short line per part. Do not repeat every label already on the figure."
      }
